<title>JAPAN: Japan to cooperate with G7 to stablise markets - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan to cooperate with G7 to stablise markets - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan will continue to cooperate closely with the Group of Seven (G7) nations to bring about stability in international financial markets, Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka told parliament on Friday.  </p>
<p>&quot;We will continue to cooperate closely with the finance ministers of the (G7) nations through our G7 meetings to stabilise international financial markets,&quot; Mitsuzuka said.</p>
<p>He also said the government will push ahead with its &quot;Big Bang&quot; reforms of Tokyo's financial markets so that Tokyo will be able to function as a key international financial centre.</p>
</text>
